#  aacpack's sec family at level -1: section_data.  kd 0 the bits of a
#  section's codebook (a tree: the node is where in it), 1 whether the
#  section goes on to the next band (in the order of the section data after
#  the spectra, Model's f_CS: of a run of bands of a kind, its kind and how
#  far it goes), 2 (f_CS) whether a section starts at the band, 3 (f_CS) a
#  coded section's codebook after the spectra (the tree); cb the section's
#  codebook (16 not yet), pc the one before it in the group (16 none), fc
#  the band's in the channel's last frame (16 not known), gc in the group
#  before (16 none), oc of the CPE's other channel (16 none), sb the band,
#  run the section's bands so far, rem those left to max_sfb, ws the window
#  sequence, gr the group, fn the last frame's codebook at the next band (16
#  not known), mu the band's ms_used (1 L/R, 2 M/S; 0 none), ob the first
#  channel's section start at the band (1 no, 2 yes; 0 none), dm the
#  digest's prediction (0 none); f_CS: pr what the encoder the sections have
#  been most like predicts (2: 1 + a start there + 2 x how many of the other
#  two agree; 3: 1 + its codebook; 0 none), pt (2) 1 + the three encoders'
#  starts as bits, (3) 1 + how many of the other two give its codebook + 3
#  if its section is this one, ch (3) 1 + the codebook that takes the fewest
#  bits for the section's values, bq how well that encoder has done lately
#  (1 none of its last few hundred bands wrong, 2 under 1%, 3 under 10%, 4
#  more; 0 none) (cbsel.inc).
#  IDX/IDX-FORMAT.md is the format; ../../mk.sh regenerates MOD/l9 from
#  this file and family.inc.

Prefix H1_sec
Debug 1
Const 0

Index a
 a_kd: kd, 1!111
 a_oc: oc, 1!1111111111111111
 a_pc: pc, 1!111
 a_mu: mu, 1!11
 a_pr: pr, 1!1111111111111111

Index b
 b_kd: kd, 1!111
 b_gc: gc, 1!1111111111111111
 b_ws: ws, 1!111
 b_ch: ch, 1!111111111111

Index c
 c_kd: kd, 1!111
 c_run: run, 1!1111111111111111
 c_cb: cb, 1!1111111111111111
 c_ch: ch, 1!111111111111

Index d
 d_kd: kd, 1!111
 d_pc: pc, 1!1111111111111111
 d_fc: fc, 1!1111111111111111
 d_pr: pr, 1!1111111111111111

Index m
 m_kd: kd, 1!111
 m_bq: bq, 1!1111
 m_pr: pr, 1!111111

Index t

Index g

Number rA, 1, 0!11111111
Number rB, 1, 0!11111111
Number rC, 1, 0!11101010
Number rD, 1, 0!11111110
Number lr, 1, 0!01111
Number mwA, 1, 0!00010100
Number mwB, 1, 0!00011111
Number mwC, 1, 0!00000000
Number mwD, 1, 0!00001000
Number mb, 1, 0!00100000
#  Frozen: what a family of bit() decisions never reads: no mantissa, no
#  hint, no signs.
! Number rT, 1, 0!00000000
! Number mwT, 1, 0!00000000
! Number mt, 1, 0!000
! Number rG, 1, 0!00000000
! Number mwG, 1, 0!00000000
#  Rows per table, as log2: a table whose index Volume fits in 2^h rows is
#  direct, one that does not is hashed into 2^h rows.  Frozen.
! Number hA, 1, 0!11000
! Number hB, 1, 0!11000
! Number hC, 1, 0!11000
! Number hD, 1, 0!11000
! Number hM, 1, 0!11000
! Number hT, 1, 0!11000
